# Resolutions

This directory holds board resolutions and meeting action packages for
{{ org_name }}, using the `RES-NNN` identifier scheme described in
`GOVERNANCE.md`, Section 9.

## What belongs here

- Adopted resolutions: elections, officer appointments, policy adoptions
  and amendments, financial authorizations, and any other formal board
  action that isn't itself a full policy or bylaws document.
- Omnibus meeting action packages that bundle several resolutions
  considered at a single meeting into one {{ mr_term }}.

## How resolutions get here

A director or officer proposes a resolution by opening {{ "an" if vcs_platform == "gitlab" else "a" }}
{{ mr_term }} on a `board/` branch with the exact resolution text in the
{{ mr_abbr }} description, per `GOVERNANCE.md`. Approval at the required
quorum threshold and merge to `main` constitute adoption; the merge commit
timestamp is the official adoption date, not any date written in the
document.

## A note on privacy

This directory is a scaffold. It ships empty. Real resolutions can
reference specific individuals (appointments, removals, compensation
decisions), specific dollar amounts, or other sensitive organizational
detail.

**Your organization controls its own privacy posture for its rendered
repository.** If this repository is public, or you are otherwise unsure
whether a specific resolution is appropriate for this level of visibility,
keep it in your organization's own **private** repository instead.

**Never contribute real resolutions, or any other real adopted content,
back to the [Golden Records](https://github.com/USCouncil/golden-records)
commons.** That repository is a public, generic template — it must never
receive real organization data. This directory, in *your own* rendered
repository, is the right place for your real resolutions; the commons
template is not.
